(4169306, 596463, 68504, '<td valign="top">This is the kind of photo that makes me want to start all over again, showing that photography can be art.  Most hesitantly I add that the signal ear of corn is somewhat jarring, a little out of sync with the other elements, its less attractive end in prominence and at this resolution (on my monitor?) the rest of it too blurred to give it any grace, and this is the more noticeable because the ear behind it to  the right has just enough and no more detail to suggest such grace.</td>', 'This is the kind of photo that makes me want to start all over again, showing that photography can be art.  Most hesitantly I add that the signal ear of corn is somewhat jarring, a little out of sync with the other elements, its less attractive end in prominence and at this resolution (on my monitor?) the rest of it too blurred to give it any grace, and this is the more noticeable because the ear behind it to  the right has just enough and no more detail to suggest such grace.', '2007-10-15 14:33:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4169367, 596628, 73084, '<td valign="top">Thanks so much for those who voted and left comments, even if good or bad. This was my first challenge, and to place 56th out of 120 is not all that bad for a first submission. I''ll take all feedback and maybe do better next time!</td>', 'Thanks so much for those who voted and left comments, even if good or bad. This was my first challenge, and to place 56th out of 120 is not all that bad for a first submission. I''ll take all feedback and maybe do better next time!', '2007-10-15 15:09:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4169577, 596781, 30982, '<td valign="top">You got some good comments on why this didn''t work for voters.  It looks like a good location to shoot and the basic compositional elements are there, with a few "no no''s" (cutting the head in half, for instance.)  When shooting something like this, you want to try different angles, different approaches.  Get closer, get further back, try from the side so the wall isn''t completely "flat" to the camera.  The light may be a bit bright for this setting, meaning try to shoot more toward early morning or late afternoon when the light creates more shadow and depth.  The annoying thing about trying to get good shots is we''re limited to very short periods of time when using ambient light.  I don''t see anything in your post processing that jumps out as bad or wrong, and I''m not an expert in post, so I don''t really see what to add other than possibly some proverbial dodging and burning to add texture and depth.</td>', 'You got some good comments on why this didn''t work for voters.  It looks like a good location to shoot and the basic compositional elements are there, with a few "no no''s" (cutting the head in half, for instance.)  When shooting something like this, you want to try different angles, different approaches.  Get closer, get further back, try from the side so the wall isn''t completely "flat" to the camera.  The light may be a bit bright for this setting, meaning try to shoot more toward early morning or late afternoon when the light creates more shadow and depth.  The annoying thing about trying to get good shots is we''re limited to very short periods of time when using ambient light.  I don''t see anything in your post processing that jumps out as bad or wrong, and I''m not an expert in post, so I don''t really see what to add other than possibly some proverbial dodging and burning to add texture and depth.', '2007-10-15 16:30:33.000000', NULL, 0),
